  *NOTE*: `math.greater` supports broadcasting. More about broadcasting
  [here](http://docs.scipy.org/doc/numpy/user/basics.broadcasting.html)

  Example:

  ```python
  x = tf.constant([5, 4, 6])
  y = tf.constant([5, 2, 5])
  tf.math.greater(x, y) ==> [False, True, True]

  x = tf.constant([5, 4, 6])
  y = tf.constant([5])
  tf.math.greater(x, y) ==> [False, False, True]
  ```

